            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical testing of the Sicard system for automatic evaluation of electrocardiograms].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3153-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Appraisal of the Sicard (Siemens) system for the automated evaluation of ECG's is reported. 528 ECG's were simultaneously recorded on paper and magnetic tape and examined by a group of specialists and the 404/3 computer forming part of the system, followed by a check on an IBM computer. A very high percentage of fits was noted and a favourable judgment is passed on the system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
